# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AVOXAN — Cloudflare Pages redirects
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pages auto-serves .html files at their bare path, so both
# /contact.html AND /contact work. To prevent Google from
# indexing both as duplicates, we 301 every .html URL to the
# extensionless canonical version.
#
# Format: <source> <destination> <status>
# Pages reads top-to-bottom; first match wins.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Top-level pages (.html → extensionless)
/services.html        /services        301
/pricing.html         /pricing         301
/process.html         /process         301
/faq.html             /faq             301
/contact.html         /contact         301
/index.html           /                301

# ── Case studies
/work/brightside-family-dental.html       /work/brightside-family-dental 301
/work/marin-ashby-studio.html             /work/marin-ashby-studio       301
/work/avery-reyes-law-group.html          /work/avery-reyes-law-group    301
/work/avoxan-studio-site.html             /work/avoxan-studio-site       301

# ── Field notes (blog)
/blog/website-cost-2026.html                  /blog/website-cost-2026            301
/blog/beautiful-website-no-leads.html         /blog/beautiful-website-no-leads   301
/blog/local-seo-checklist.html                /blog/local-seo-checklist          301
/blog/ai-search-citation.html                 /blog/ai-search-citation           301
/blog/webflow-wordpress-framer-2026.html      /blog/webflow-wordpress-framer-2026 301
/blog/questions-to-ask-web-designer.html      /blog/questions-to-ask-web-designer 301
/blog/chiropractor-website-teardown.html      /blog/chiropractor-website-teardown 301
/blog/wedding-photographer-teardown.html      /blog/wedding-photographer-teardown 301

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Trailing-slash canonicalization
# Cloudflare Pages doesn't auto-strip these, so Google was treating
# /services and /services/ as two separate URLs. Pick one canonical
# (no trailing slash) and redirect the other.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/services/    /services    301
/pricing/     /pricing     301
/process/     /process     301
/faq/         /faq         301
/contact/     /contact     301
/work/        /work        301
/blog/        /blog        301

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LEGACY URLs from the prior Squarespace site
# Search Console kept flagging these — old slugs Google had cached.
# Catch each pattern and 301 to the closest new equivalent.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Old home URL
/home                 /        301
/home/                /        301

# Old "case studies" / portfolio paths → /work
/case-studies         /work    301
/case-studies/        /work    301
/portfolio            /work    301
/portfolio/           /work    301
/portfolio-list-*     /work    301
/portfolio-list-*/    /work    301

# Old Squarespace blog paths → /blog
# Catches /blog-post, /blog-post1, /blog-post2, /blog-post3, ...
/blog-post            /blog    301
/blog-post/           /blog    301
/blog-post*           /blog    301
/blog-post*/          /blog    301
/blog-list            /blog    301
/blog-list/           /blog    301

# Old Squarespace service pages → /services
/web-designdevelopment    /services    301
/web-designdevelopment/   /services    301
/web-design               /services    301
/web-design/              /services    301
/development              /services    301
/development/             /services    301
/seo                      /services    301
/seo/                     /services    301

# Common Squarespace leftovers — cheap insurance
/about                /                  301
/about/               /                  301
/about-us             /                  301
/about-us/            /                  301
/work-with-us         /contact           301
/work-with-us/        /contact           301
/get-started          /contact           301
/get-started/         /contact           301
